# Side by side
table = vendor,fraud caught,good transactions wrongly blocked,fee per 1000 transactions,integration,live before freeze; **Tollgate**,91.2%,1.9%,$4.10,6 weeks,Go; Vantage Shield,94.8%,3.1%,$6.80,10 weeks,No-go; Kestrel Risk,89.5%,1.2%,$2.90,4 weeks,Go

# Annual fees
data fees = vendor,annual fee; Tollgate,295200; Vantage Shield,489600; Kestrel Risk,208800
chart hbar fees unit=$ focus="Tollgate" title="Annual fees at 6M transactions a month"

# What the trade-off means
Each wrongly blocked transaction is a real customer declined at checkout.
- Vantage Shield catches 3.6 points more fraud than Tollgate.
- It also wrongly blocks 1.2 points more good transactions, and costs $194,400 more a year.
- Kestrel Risk blocks the fewest good customers and is cheapest, but catches 1.7 points less fraud than Tollgate.

# Recommendation
We lean toward **Tollgate** as the balanced choice. **Kestrel Risk** is the budget fallback if the steering group wants to cut fees by about $86,400 a year.

!! Sign by 2026-12-15 to have Tollgate or Kestrel Risk live before the 2027-02-01 change freeze. Vantage Shield cannot make the freeze.
